+This is a pure-Python reimplementation of `packignore`, the legacy exclusion
+engine. docs/PACKIGNORE.md describes the basics; the rules below are what the
+engine actually does, including the parts the docs leave out.
+
+The tree
+--------
+The engine sees the regular files under the root (symlinks and special files
+are skipped, as is a `.git` directory directly under the root), visited in
+`os.walk` order. It stores them on a case-insensitive, normalization-insensitive
+filesystem: two paths whose components are canonically caseless-equal
+(NFD + full case folding) are the same entry. The first path seen supplies the
+name; the last one supplies the content and mode. A file colliding with a
+directory is an error, and so are a file name that is not valid UTF-8 and a
+second hard link to the same file.
+
+.packignore syntax
+------------------
+- The file is UTF-8 (strict, no BOM handling) and split with str.splitlines().
+  Each line is str.strip()ped. Empty lines and lines starting with `;` are
+  skipped. `#` is NOT a comment.
+- A leading `!` negates (re-includes); the rest of the line is the pattern,
+  taken as is.
+- Trailing `/`s mean "directories only" and are removed. Leading `/`s are
+  removed. If the pattern contains a `/` (including a removed leading one) it
+  is anchored: matched against the whole path relative to the directory
+  holding the .packignore. Otherwise it matches a file or directory name at
+  any depth below that directory.
+- `*` matches any run of characters except `/`, `?` exactly one. A path
+  segment that is exactly `**` matches zero to three segments (not more: the
+  engine has always capped it). Everything else,
+  including `[`, `]` and `\\`, is literal. Matching is case-sensitive.
+- After the above, `{a,b}` groups are expanded: a group runs from a `{` to
+  the next `}` (no nesting; an unclosed `{` is literal), alternatives are
+  split on `,`, and expansion continues in the rest of the pattern. `!`,
+  trailing/leading `/` and anchoring are decided for the whole line, before
+  expansion.
+
+Precedence
+----------
+A file is decided by the deepest path (the file itself, else its nearest
+ancestor directory) that any pattern matches. Among the patterns matching that
+path, the winner is the one from the deepest .packignore, then the one with
+the most literal characters (counted over the whole line before brace
+expansion: everything except `*`, `?`, `/`, `{`, `}` and `,`), then the
+last one in the file. A negated winner keeps the path, any other winner
+excludes it.
+
+If no pattern matches the file itself, it is still excluded when it is
+executable (any x bit) or its first line (up to the first b"\\n") contains
+`@generated`.
+
+A .packignore is read only if the directory holding it is not excluded (the
+root's always is). Being excluded itself does not stop it from being read.
+A .packignore that would be read but is a directory, or is not valid UTF-8,
+is an error.
